// onsa.toml
// [test]
// mode = "parse"
// spec = ["§2.5", "§4.5"]

// The functions of negative/nesting_type_args_expr_sum_over.onsa one level shallower (S-332, §2.5,
// §4.5): the height of `::[…]` in an expression is the height of its receiver plus one plus the height
// of its list of types, so each `let g = …` here is exactly 256 levels deep, the deepest the limit
// accepts, and nothing is reported. A count that took a level too many (the list counted on top of
// the receiver and the `::[` counted twice, say) would give E0006 here. The file reads the syntax only
// (`mode = "parse"`).

